DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260820T181500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260820T201500
SUMMARY:NEW Korean x English Language Exchange\, Class & Board Games (LIMI
 TED SPACE) 
DESCRIPTION:Toronto's BIGGEST Language Exchange Social Event + Class\n**KO
 REAN x ENGLISH** Language Exchange + Mini English Class with Teacher + Boa
 rd Games @ Café Princess\n\nEvent & Class organized by **TILE** (Toronto 
 International Language Exchange)\n\n**.⚠️ Space is VERY limited\,** so
  reserve your spot early! **We can only accept a limited number of partici
 pants due to space limitations.**\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-
 \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\n**Come on time f
 or 6:15 PM** & please RSVP while there are still spots remaining.\n\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-
 \\-\\-\\-\n\n**📍 Location:**\n**Café Princess**\n**5590 Yonge Street\,
  North York**\n**Just steps from FINCH SUBWAY STATION**\n\n**✨ This firs
 t class is FREE!**\n**Simply buy 1 item from the Café Princess menu to pa
 rticipate. Popular menu items include:**\n\n* *🍓 Strawberry Cheesecake 
 Bingsu*\n* *🍧 Mango or Oreo Bingsu*\n* *☕ Matcha & Tiramisu Lattes*\n
 * *🧇 Princess Waffles with Ice Cream & Much More*\n\n### **What to Expe
 ct**\n\n* *🇰🇷 Guided Korean & English language practice*\n* *📚 In
 teractive mini-lesson led by an award-winning certified teacher*\n* *🗣
 ️ Structured conversation activities with native and fluent speakers*\n*
  *🎲 Board games and social activities to practice language naturally*\n
 * *🤝 Make new friends while improving your communication skills*\n\n###
  **Event Details**\n\n* *📅 Date: Thursday\, August 20\, 2026*\n* *🕡 
 Time: 6:15 PM – 8:15 PM*\n\n### **Learn From an Expert Teacher**\n\n* *A
 ward-winning Certified Language Teacher*\n* *OCT\, MA\, HBA\, BEd\, EELC (
 University of Toronto - Rotman)*\n* *PhD Researcher (University of Toronto
  – OISE)*\n* *Founder & President of TILE Learning*\n\n### **Who Should 
 Attend?**\n\n* *English learners (ESL)*\n* *Native Korean speakers wanting
  to practice English*\n* *Korean learners of all levels*\n* *International
  students\, newcomers\, professionals\, and anyone interested in language 
 and culture*\n\n**Feel free to e-mail [info@tilelearning.com](mailto:info@
 tilelearning.com) if you have any questions.**\n**Check out our [website](
 https://www.tilelearning.com/) and [instagram](https://www.instagram.com/t
 ilelearning/) accounts for more details.**
